From a9d1bded589e740f193913205e82c96c3376c98c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:50:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: share GDM and PPE infrastructure with EcoNet

Keep the EN7523/EN7581 and EN751221 QDMA datapaths in separate
airoha-eth and econet-eth modules, while moving their common GDM,
phylink and flow-offload interfaces into airoha-common.

Add an EN751221 backend to the common PPE frontend.  The newer Airoha
backend accesses NPU services only through optional host callbacks, so
the common module and the EcoNet driver do not depend on airoha-npu.

Model both EcoNet GDM ports as child netdevs using the common phylink
infrastructure.  This allows GDM1 to act as the DSA conduit for an
MT7530 switch through ethernet = <&gdm1>, while GDM2 remains available
for a direct PHY, WAN or xPON datapath.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI <openai@example.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
